      capabilities: 'Authorization is a flat set of four capabilities: read (view data), trade (place trades, propose proposals, send proposal messages), manage (admin operations: approve/decline proposals, create/void markets, edit groups, edit non-lifecycle workspace settings), manage_workspace (lifecycle operations: delete the workspace, change visibility, configure auto-fund, set default proposal liquidity). manage_workspace is granular and not implied by manage; the workspace creator holds it implicitly, the seeded Admin group holds it by default, and any group can be granted or revoked it via PUT /api/groups/:id. Each permission group carries a capabilities[] array; a caller\'s effective capabilities are the union across every group they belong to in the current workspace. Legacy role labels (admin, agent, member) seen in responses are derived for display and are not authoritative.',
